# Incremental Implementation

Build in small increments. Implement one piece, verify it, then expand. Each increment should leave the project in a working state.

## Increment Cycle

1. Implement the smallest complete piece.
2. Run the smallest relevant verification.
3. Fix failures that are clearly within scope.
4. Record what changed and what was verified.
5. Continue to the next slice.

## Scope Discipline

Do not clean up unrelated code, refactor adjacent areas, add features outside the spec, or introduce abstractions for hypothetical future use. Note unrelated issues separately.

## Slicing Strategies

- Vertical slice: one complete user path.
- Contract-first: shared API/types first when frontend and backend depend on each other.
- Risk-first: prove uncertain integrations, performance paths, or data flows early.

## Verification

After each meaningful increment, run the relevant test, typecheck, lint, build, or manual check. Do not repeat the same command on unchanged code just for reassurance.
